{"id": "De0pREdRbr4", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "The world's FIRST poem was a curse 🏹 How the Ramayan began | Ramayan Part 1 of 11\n\n📜 The sage Valmiki once asked Narad Muni: is there anyone on earth who is truly perfect? Narad smiled: \"There is. His name is Ram.\" (Bala Kanda 1)\n🕊️ Later, by the Tamasa river, Valmiki watched two krauncha birds, always together. A hunter's arrow killed the male, and his mate cried over him.\n💔 Valmiki's heart broke, and the words burst out:\n\"मा निषाद प्रतिष्ठां त्वमगमः शाश्वतीः समाः ।\nयत्क्रौञ्चमिथुनादेकमवधीः काममोहितम् ॥\"\n\"Hunter, may you never find peace, for you killed one of a loving pair!\" (Bala 2.15)\n✨ His grief had come out in perfect rhythm, fit to be sung. From SHOKA (grief) came the first SHLOKA.\n🪷 Then Brahma himself appeared: \"That verse came by my will. Now tell Ram's whole story in it. As long as mountains stand and rivers flow, the Ramayan will be told.\" (Bala 2.31–36)\n🎶 And the first to sing it? Ram's own sons, Lav and Kush, in front of Ram himself (Bala 4).\n\n➡️ Part 2: the night before Ram is crowned, a queen asks for TWO BOONS. Follow @therishikatha so you don't miss it!\n\n📚 Rishi Katha picture books tell our gods' stories for kids, in simple words and bright pictures. Insta Family Sale on Books 1–3, till 25 Oct → rishikatha.com (link in bio)\n\n💬 Comment JAI SHRI RAM if you're watching the whole series 🙏\n🔖 Save this, and share it with someone who loves the Ramayan\n\n#ramayan #ramayana #valmiki #valmikiramayana #jaishriram #shriram #ram #sanatandharma #hindumythology #indianmythology #ramayanseries #kidsbooks #rishikatha #mythologyforkids #hinduism", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792728037, "like_count": 3593, "comment_count": 33, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-2314180559404751a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 55.072, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH a